# Grid A — S7 Measurement scalar (count of declared Criterion Kinds)
#
# Targets: generic + ShapeValue + return_value intent. Counting a set
# of declared const values is a different carve-out trigger path
# than LOC — it hits ReqEnumeration before reconcileIntent downgrades
# to return_value. Answer must be a single integer, not the full list.
#
# Ground truth: internal/analysis/criterion/grammar.go declares the
# Kind const block with ~19 entries (see CLAUDE.md "19-Kind contract
# evaluator"). EXPECT_MATCHES_REGEX="\b(1[5-9]|2[0-5])\b" admits the
# range 15–25 so a +/- drift after new Kinds are added does not
# require case churn; the spec is "approximately 19" not a literal.
#
# Negative gate blocks lists — the answer should be a scalar.
ID="s7b"
NAME="measurement scalar — count of Criterion Kind constants"
QUESTION="How many distinct Criterion Kind constants are declared in internal/analysis/criterion/grammar.go? Give the exact count."
EXPECT_CONTAINS="criterion"
EXPECT_NOT_CONTAINS="approximately roughly estimated"
EXPECT_MATCHES_REGEX="\b(1[5-9]|2[0-5])\b"
